invariant: INV-7
file: quic.c
catches: quic_driver_test
reason: ch_quic_switch_version takes a switch after the ServerHello step,
  once a delivery of no bytes at the Handshake level has emptied cfg.buf,
  so the Handshake keys installed under version 1 stay while the packet
  calls hold every Handshake packet to version 2. The server's CRYPTO
  bytes fixed the negotiated version when they arrived
  (rfc9369.txt:236-244). test/quic_version_tests.h requires CH_EINVAL
  there, with t.pt_len at 0 so the step is the only condition left.

--- old
           q->step == HSQ_STEP_AWAIT_SERVER_HELLO && q->t.pt_len == 0 &&
--- new
           q->t.pt_len == 0 &&
